o stretch. If those belly muscles are full of stitches, staples, and healing tissue, stretching them causes excruciating pain right in the stomach. To avoid ripping their stomach open and causing that pain, the person will naturally fold forward into a fetal position. You cannot walk effectively if you are folded in half. **The Takeaway** In this scenario, the legs and spine do not need to heal, because they were never hurt. It is the *belly* that needs to heal. Physical therapy in this case isn't about fixing the legs or the spine; it is about gently stretching the stomach wounds and retraining the belly muscles to act like strong "ropes" again so the person can stand up straight without agonizing stomach pain.
